    {
      "question": "e-14407",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "5ab10c752f27868cc0b05926176559d6160a3bf24605413d0656b578f0b2a633",
      "new_sha256": "a50c9efca0e1031aec97db7313c550fddcaa0c31f4bf5b0ec248a1754df57efb",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-14407",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=-2x^2.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-4x\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n-4 \\, \\textrm{d}u=16x \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt {\\ln 4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-2\\ln 4$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}}16x{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}}{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}\\cdot 16x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}{e}^{u}\\cdot (-4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4{e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}\u20614} \\\\  & =-4({e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{1}{16}-1) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{15}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009212/example-14407.json",
          "file_sha256": "ba6830c3489bf593519e7a7b63fde36873baa022b41e8a8b41a35f5fdb972c5f"
        }
